<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Basic HTML Web Page</title>

    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
            background: linear-gradient(to right, #4facfe, #00f2fe);
        }

        .container {
            width: 70%;
            margin: 50px auto;
            background-color: white;
            padding: 30px;
            border-radius: 15px;
            box-shadow: 0px 0px 15px gray;
        }

        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            color: darkblue;
        }

        h2 {
            text-align: center;
            color: darkgreen;
        }

        h3 {
            text-align: center;
            color: crimson;
        }

        p {
            font-size: 18px;
            line-height: 1.8;
            text-align: justify;
        }

        hr {
            border: 2px solid steelblue;
        }

        .footer {
            margin-top: 20px;
            text-align: center;
            background-color: darkblue;
            color: white;
            padding: 12px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
    </style>

</head>

<body>

    <div class="container">

        <h1>Welcome to HTML</h1>
        <h2>Experiment 1: Creating a Basic HTML Web Page</h2>

        <hr>

        <p>
            HTML stands for <b>HyperText Markup Language</b>. It is used to create
            <i>web pages</i> and display content on the internet.
        </p>

        <p>
            This text is <u>underlined</u>.<br>
            This line is displayed after a line break.
        </p>

        <p>
            Mathematical Formula:
            x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> = z<sup>2</sup>
        </p>

        <p>
            Chemical Formula:
            H<sub>2</sub>O and CO<sub>2</sub>
        </p>

        <hr>

        <h3>Thank You!</h3>

        <div class="footer">
            Created by: Lakshmi | Basic HTML Web Page
        </div>

    </div>

</body>
</html>
